    thinking: "**Evolving Categories System**\n\nI\'m working on enabling custom categories. The current `CATEGORIES` array constant will be replaced with state using `useState`. This will allow users to dynamically add and manage their own categories, adding greater flexibility to the application.\n\n\n**Refining Category Implementation**\n\nI\'ve made progress on the category implementation, now I am considering how to handle the \"All\" category. Currently, it\'s distinct, but I\'m thinking of either keeping it separate or prepending it to the list. Furthermore, I\'ve incorporated the UI requirements for adding new categories, envisioning a \"+ Add\" button within the category scrollable row. This approach should allow a user to more easily add categories.\n\n\n**Considering Category Input**\n\nI\'m now thinking about where the \"Add Category\" input or button should live. Should it be a distinct button within the existing category selection bottom sheet, or perhaps integrated into the \"Add Snippet\" form itself? I\'m evaluating the UI implications of both approaches.\n\n\n**Implementing Category Input**\n\nI\'ve decided to integrate the category input directly into the \"Add Snippet\" form. My idea is to have a \"+ New\" button that morphs into an inline input field when clicked, using state to manage the input\'s visibility and value. I\'m exploring an `autoFocus` property for the input and a \"submit\" button alongside the input field. I am also planning on updating the category list and setting the form category if the user enters a new category.\n\n\n**Refining Custom Category Emoji**\n\nI\'m now implementing the default emoji for custom categories. I\'ve updated the `getCategoryEmoji` function to provide a \"\360\237\217\267\357\270\217\" as the default for new, user-defined categories. Also, I am now updating the `CATEGORIES` array.\n```\n\n\n**Updating UI States**\n\nI\'ve been working on managing the UI state with `useState`. I am using state variables for things like: the current snippets, a list of categories, the selected category, the search query, and the state of the bottom sheet. In addition to this, I\'m handling the state for the current snippet, including: title, category, and body. I\'m hoping this will provide a clear separation of concerns in how the state is managed.\n\n\n**Managing Category Counts**\n\nI\'m now focusing on efficiently updating category counts. I\'ve switched from using the `CATEGORIES` constant to the `categories` state variable in the `useMemo` hook, ensuring accurate counts reflecting the dynamically added categories. This is key for the tab navigation.\n\n\n**Refactoring Category Array**\n\nI\'m now refactoring the `CATEGORIES` array constant to improve how the categories are handled and displayed. I\'ve updated the mapping logic in `page.tsx` to use `[\'All\', ...categories]` instead of the old constant, ensuring that the dynamically updated category list is properly used. I am currently focusing on how to update this array.\n\n\n**Revising Category Handling**\n\nI\'m now revising the category display within the \"Add Snippet\" form. I\'m updating the mapping logic to handle a dynamic `categories` array, not a constant. I\'m refactoring the UI to render the category buttons, ensuring proper selection and styling. I am also currently working on getting the emoji to show up correctly for the currently selected category.\n\n\n**Implementing Category Selection**\n\nI\'m now implementing the dynamic category selection in the \"Add Snippet\" form using the provided JSX. I\'m focusing on rendering category buttons from the dynamic `categories` array. I will use the `isSelected` variable to apply styling and ensure the `setFormCategory` function updates the UI. I am getting the category emoji in this step as well.\n\n\n**Implementing Category Input Field**\n\nI\'m now integrating a dynamic category input field. I am adding an input field and logic within the \"Add Snippet\" form to create new categories. I\'m handling the \"Enter\" key to add the new category to the `categories` array and setting the form category. I am also making sure that the escape key can properly cancel the field.\n\n\n**Finalizing Category Input**\n\nI am now finalizing the category input field\'s functionality. I\'ve integrated a \"Save\" button to add the new category to the list, which updates the UI and sets the form\'s category. I also ensure that the input is trimmed before submission, avoiding empty or duplicate entries. I am handling state updates, and ensuring that the component displays the currently selected category with its emoji.\n\n\n"
