  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Color Strategies**\n\nI\'m currently focused on streamlining color management. My current thought is to either adopt semantic Tailwind classes via `globals.css`, or utilize the `dark:` prefix directly in the markup. I\'m leaning toward implementing the latter using either regex or manual string replacements for the dark mode adjustments.\n\n\n**Implementing Dark Mode**\n\nI\'ve realized enabling dark mode in the Tailwind configuration might not be necessary. I can directly utilize the `dark:` variant classes like `dark:bg-[#111827]`, which is working well with the default media query. Now, I\'m identifying the color conversions needed. I\'m noting specific color mappings like `bg-[#E2E8F0]` to `dark:bg-[#0B0F19]` for the root body and `bg-white` to `dark:bg-[#1E293B]` for components. I\'m also capturing text color conversions, like `text-[#1F2937]` to `dark:text-[#F3F4F6]`.\n\n\n**Mapping Color Variations**\n\nI\'m now expanding my dark mode mappings beyond the initial examples. I\'ve noted conversions like `subdued` to `dark:text-[#9CA3AF]`, and various border colors. I\'m also addressing the gray-50 hover states and empty button backgrounds in dark mode. Moreover, I\'m refactoring the inline `body` styles, including adding a media query for the dark scheme.\n\n\n**Simplifying Body Styles**\n\nI\'ve decided to streamline the inline styles for the body wrapper. Instead of modifying the style object directly, I\'m refactoring it to leverage Tailwind classes. Specifically, I\'m converting the `background: \'#E2E8F0\'` to use `bg-[#E2E8F0] dark:bg-[#0B0F19]`. I\'m now applying these class names to the `div` element in `app/page.tsx`, to improve the visual theme support.\n\n\n**Enhancing Global Styles**\n\nI\'m now integrating new styles into the `globals.css` file. I\'ve added a font family and ensured tap highlights are transparent. I\'m also including styling for a flexbox container, while centering and ensuring a minimum viewport height. I\'ve directly included the media query for dark mode within the stylesheet. I am also planning on converting all instances of specific color combinations to use a consistent `dark:` variant and updating the overall text and background styling.\n\n\n**Optimizing Element Styling**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the styling for specific elements. I\'m converting inline style attributes to Tailwind classes. For example, I\'m transforming direct width and height declarations, background colors, and flexbox configurations into concise, responsive Tailwind equivalents with dark mode variants where needed. I\'m also addressing ring and shadow styles for improved visual consistency.\n\n\n**Refining UI Component Styling**\n\nI\'m now methodically updating UI components with Tailwind classes. I\'m focusing on the header and search input, converting inline styles to include dark mode variants. For the header, this includes background, border, and text colors. With the search input, I\'m adjusting text, background, and border colors, as well as the text color of the icon.\n\n\n**Styling Components with Tailwind**\n\nI\'m currently working to incorporate Tailwind classes into the UI components. For the search input, I\'m refactoring the classes for the focus state, transition, shadow, and placeholder colors. I\'m also addressing the clear search button and category chips, updating the colors and styles to fit with the existing color variants and the focus states. I\'m also ensuring the components have consistent colors and shadows.\n\n\n**Updating Empty State**\n\nI\'m now styling the empty state component for the snippet list to match the visual theme. I\'ve updated the text, using consistent color variants. I\'m also now adjusting the background using the correct Tailwind classes, ensuring a harmonious visual flow between light and dark modes. I\'m also making adjustments to the icon styling to ensure it is visible and clear on all themes.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Refactoring Snippet Cards**\n\nI\'m currently updating the snippet cards to reflect the changes. I\'m ensuring the light and dark mode classes are appropriately set, using Tailwind variants to manage the color changes. I\'ve also refactored the classes for the borders, specifically for the copied state, to use a more concise approach.\n\n\n**Updating Text Elements**\n\nI\'m now applying dark mode variants to all text elements within the snippet component. I\'m focusing on the `h3`, `p`, and `span` tags, updating the text color with `dark:` variants. I\'m also addressing the text and border colors within the actions section, like the edit and delete buttons, ensuring a cohesive dark mode appearance.\n\n\n**Styling Bottom Sheet**\n\nI\'m now incorporating Tailwind classes for the bottom sheet and its backdrop. I\'m focusing on the backdrop\'s background color and opacity using `dark:` variants and transition effects. For the bottom sheet modal, I\'m addressing the background, border radius, padding, shadow, and transition. Also, I am adjusting the \"grabber\" styling, converting its background color to use light and dark variants to better support the theme.\n\n\n**Applying Dark Mode Variants**\n\nI\'m now integrating dark mode variants into form elements. For labels, I\'m using `dark:text-[#D1D5DB]`. Inputs are receiving `dark:border-[#334155]` and `dark:bg-[#0F172A]` classes, along with appropriate text color variants. I\'m also updating the bottom sheet\'s close button, setting both the background and text color to support light and dark modes. I\'m focusing on ensuring visual consistency across all form components.\n\n\n**Updating Category Styling**\n\nI\'m now refining the category modal button\'s visual appearance using Tailwind. I\'m focusing on the selected and unselected states, adjusting background, border, text, and shadow classes for both light and dark modes. I\'m also addressing the \"add category\" button\'s inline view. I\'m updating the internal input, ensuring a consistent dark mode variant and applying the updated styling to `font-[\'Nunito_Sans\',sans-serif]`, as well as applying it to the border color.\n\n\n**Refining Input Styling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the styling of input elements within forms, like the message input, in light of the last thought process. The input\'s border is getting updated to use light and dark variants to provide a consistent visual look. Also, the label and button styling, including hover states, are getting reviewed to maintain theme coherence. I am also planning on updating the font families used.\n\n\n**Enhancing Form Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating dark mode variants into form elements. I\'ve updated the border styling for form inputs, including light and dark mode variants, and updated the text and background color of the save button and ensured its interactivity state changes as needed to provide a smooth user experience. I am also planning on updating the font families used.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
