  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Database Solutions**\n\nI\'m now exploring database options. The original thought of using SQLite poses an issue given the application\'s Cloud Run deployment \342\200\223 the ephemeral nature of SQLite storage in a containerized environment is problematic for secure content. I\'m now looking at alternatives for persistent data storage that are better suited for this architecture, such as cloud-based database services.\n\n\n**Analyzing Persistence Strategies**\n\nI\'ve considered that Cloud Run\'s ephemeral nature makes SQLite problematic without persistent volumes, which aren\'t readily available here. Client-side storage like `localStorage` or `IndexedDB` seems appropriate for personal, single-user apps. However, the user wants \"safe content.\" If they specifically requested SQLite, and if they mean a server-side DB, that\'s possible. I\'ll need to explain the limitations.\n\n\n**Evaluating Local Storage Options**\n\nI\'m now leaning heavily towards utilizing `localStorage` or `IndexedDB` for client-side persistence, given the application\'s nature as a serverless web app within a container. My preference is to implement this directly, explaining that it ensures secure, locally-saved content inherent to a PWA\'s design. I\'m exploring the option of explaining that SQLite on the server would require user accounts and remote hosting, making local storage a superior fit. I\'ve also found `sql.js` and `wa-sqlite`, but those don\'t seem right.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 683177442
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
