  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Features**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the core features: \"Export/Import\" using JSON and \"Share\" via encoded URLs. I need to nail down the specifics of these features before moving on. I am reviewing the best way to structure the JSON and encode the data for shareable URLs.\n\n\n**Implementing the Features**\n\nNow, I\'m working through the implementation design. Exporting will create a JSON blob with snippets and categories, downloadable via an anchor tag. For import, a hidden file input will read and validate the JSON. Sharing will encode the snippet and category data, appending to the URL as a query or hash. I\'ll need to handle category syncing during import/share. I\'m also planning to add the export/import and share buttons to the settings sidebar.\n\n\n**Refining Share Implementation**\n\nI\'m now refining the share functionality, specifically URL parameter handling. I\'ll decode data from `location.hash` (or `?data=`), seamlessly merge it with existing data, and display a toast notification like \"Imported from link!\". I\'m considering using `window.history.replaceState` to clear the URL parameter after import to prevent repeated imports on refresh. Since there may be an iFrame and browser restrictions, I will stick to simple notifications. This is a simple app, so a silent merge is good. I am planning to implement the required import/export functions, and update the load data `useEffect`.\n\n\n**Designing the Sidebar**\n\nI\'m now focusing on UI updates, specifically integrating buttons for export, import, and share into the \"Settings\" sidebar. I\'ll need to link these buttons to the appropriate actions. I\'m also ensuring the import logic, whether from file or URL, properly handles new, unique IDs for incoming snippets and merges categories.\n\n\n**Optimizing the Encoding**\n\nI\'ve been working on optimizing the data encoding for sharing. I\'ve found a simpler standard approach for short JSON strings, using `btoa` and `atob`. I am now leaning toward using a JSON string, then encoding it with `btoa`, then decoding with `atob`. I also need to make sure to account for URL encoding, which is an important step.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Implementation**\n\nNow I\'m finalizing the export and import functions. I have the download feature with `createElement(\'a\')`, `link.href`, and `link.download` working. Import uses a hidden file input to read and validate the JSON using a `FileReader` and `JSON.parse`. Error handling is also implemented. I use `mergeData` to handle the data merging, and toast notifications report success or errors. The file input value is also cleared after import.\n\n\n**Refining the Share Function**\n\nI\'ve been improving the share function. I am now using `JSON.stringify` to serialize the snippets and categories. Then, I am using a `btoa` encoding to produce a URL. I am using `unescape(encodeURIComponent(dataStr))` for safe base64 encoding. I\'ve also implemented error handling to provide a user-friendly toast if the data is too large.\n\n\n**Refining the Merge**\n\nI\'m now refining the data merging logic to handle incoming snippets and categories correctly. I\'m adding an `id` to new snippets to avoid conflicts and ensuring categories exist during the merge. I\'m also addressing the issue of duplicate categories. I\'m updating the `useEffect` hook to handle URL parameters for data loading, managing the `?data=` parameter, and updating `newCats`.\n\n\n**Evaluating the Merge**\n\nI\'m now evaluating the best approach to handle the data merge from shareable links. I will be considering the best way to merge, replace, or update existing local data. It seems sensible to merge the incoming data with the existing local data to avoid accidental data loss, as the user might intend to use the link to share a new setup. I\'m focusing on ensuring the proper merging of snippets and categories.\n\n\n**Refining the Categorization**\n\nI\'m now refining the category merging logic in the data merge from the shareable links. I\'m ensuring unique categories are added, and that new snippets are assigned a new ID. I am also making sure that categories are properly merged or created.\n\n\n\n**Finalizing the Integration**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating the latest changes. I\'m focusing on the final merge and URL cleanup. I am ensuring that after importing data from a share link, a toast notification confirms the successful import. I am using `window.history.replaceState` to clear the URL parameters and prevent repeated imports on refresh. Error handling is included to manage data parsing issues and provide helpful console logs. I\'m also ensuring the correct logic of the saved data.\n\n\n**Refining the useEffect**\n\nI\'m now optimizing the `useEffect` hook. I realized that keeping the data merge logic within the same initial `useEffect` is clearer and avoids race conditions, especially regarding the `setIsDataLoaded` state. This consolidated approach handles both local and linked data loading efficiently.\n\n\n\n**Evaluating the User Interface**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user interface details, particularly the new export, import, and share buttons. I need to make sure the placement of the buttons is good for the user, and that they look appealing. I\'m making sure that the buttons fit in well with the current look and feel. I am checking the current look and feel, and am now making sure that the new elements feel unified.\n\n\n**Updating the UX**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user interface details. I\'m finalizing the integration of the share link copy feature, making sure it works seamlessly. I\'m also now making sure that the new elements feel unified. I need to make sure the placement of the buttons is good for the user, and that they look appealing. I\'m integrating the fileInputRef and the new `useEffect` hook handling `URLSearchParams`. I need to ensure that the code doesn\'t produce an error.\n\n\n**Refining the UI**\n\nI\'m now refining the UI. I\'m focusing on the refactor. I am now working on the multi-edit feature, ensuring imports and initialization for `fileInputRef` function correctly. I\'m focusing on the `useEffect` hook for data loading and the merging functions.\n\n\n**Refactoring the Hook**\n\nI\'m now refactoring the `useEffect` hook. I realized the importance of consolidating data loading, and share link handling. I\'m focusing on cleaning up the code by making it more readable and efficient.\n\n\n**Consolidating Data Handling**\n\nI\'m now consolidating data handling to ensure robust merging of snippets and categories. I\'m focusing on parsing and validating the incoming data from share links. I\'m ensuring that categories from the shared data are merged, and creating new snippets. I\'m making sure new snippet IDs don\'t conflict, and updating the local categories correctly.\n\n\n**Integrating the Handlers**\n\nI\'m now integrating the data-loading and share link handlers. I\'m focusing on ensuring robust handling of incoming data. My focus is the `useEffect` hook to merge share data, and the local data. I\'m adding a robust import data handler, merging snippets and categories, with `localStorage`. I\'m making sure new snippet IDs don\'t conflict, and updating the local categories correctly.\n\n\n**Implementing Feedback**\n\nI\'m now implementing toast feedback for both successful and error scenarios. I\'ve set up a system to display temporary messages, triggered after an action such as import or export. I am ensuring that these messages disappear after a short delay and clear the current timer if new messages arrive.\n\n\n**Refining the Exports**\n\nI\'m now refining the export process to include feedback to the user. I\'ve integrated a \"Backup exported successfully\" toast notification after a successful download, ensuring that the process is clear. I\'ve also implemented error handling to provide helpful feedback in the event of any issues during the import or export process.\n\n\n**Improving the Imports**\n\nI\'m now focused on improving the data import process, focusing specifically on error handling and user feedback. I am working on using a `FileReader` to read the backup data, and handling the JSON parsing with a try/catch. I\'m making sure to trigger toast messages, displaying to the user after each import.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Share**\n\nI\'m now finalizing the share link feature. I\'ve integrated a robust copy-to-clipboard function that generates and copies the shareable URL. Error handling has been added to provide feedback if the link generation or copy fails. Additionally, I\'m integrating updates to the settings UI.\n\n\n**Enhancing the UI**\n\nI\'m now integrating UI updates to include a \"Manage Categories\" button in the settings sidebar. I\'m focusing on ensuring its functionality, proper styling, and seamless integration with the existing interface.\n\n\n**Adding the Functionality**\n\nI\'m now implementing the functionality for a multi-edit feature, and ensuring that import works correctly. I am also initializing for `fileInputRef` function, and integrating the `useEffect` hook for data loading and the merging functions.\n\n\n**Refining the Categorization**\n\nI\'m now refining the button styling and positioning, alongside error-handling improvements. I am considering best practices for implementing these updates. I am working on polishing the export and import button styles and ensuring comprehensive error messaging.\n\n\n\n**Polishing the UI**\n\nI\'m now polishing the UI and focusing on details. I\'m refining button styling, positioning, and error handling for a better user experience. I am also working on polishing the export and import button styles and ensuring comprehensive error messaging.\n\n\n\n**Reviewing the Integration**\n\nNow, I\'m reviewing `page.tsx` again to confirm alignment of all elements. I\'m making sure that the import features cover the file input element reference and modify the `useEffect` hook correctly. I\'m checking that the components align to the implementation.\n\n\n"
