  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Generating Image Concepts**\n\nI\'m working on creative image descriptions for the app, aiming for a less generic and more crafted aesthetic. Currently, I\'m focusing on abstract, lifestyle-focused image concepts that would enhance the user experience. I\'m keen on moving away from a purely AI-generated feel.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Here are a few conceptual art directions with specific image descriptions (prompts) you could use to make the app feel more human, crafted, and distinctive. \n\nYou could use these in empty states (when no search results are found or no snippets exist), as a banner above the snippets, or in the settings menu.\n\n### 1. Abstract & Tactile (Modern & Clean)\nAbstract 3D shapes or textures give the app a premium, physical feel without distracting from the text.\n*   **Prompt Idea A:** \"A macro shot of softly folded, thick textured paper in warm off-white and soft coral tones. Minimalist, elegant, soft studio lighting.\"\n*   **Prompt Idea B:** \"A 3D rendering of smooth, matte clay shapes\342\200\224a pill and a sphere\342\200\224resting on a seamless slate background. The shapes are colored in soft orange and light gray. Minimalist, tactile, clean.\"\n*   **Prompt Idea C:** \"Frosted reeded glass texture with a soft sunset glow behind it, creating blurred, warm orange and slate gray vertical lines. Elegant, premium, abstract.\"\n\n### 2. Editorial & Workspace (Human & Relatable)\nEditorial lifestyle photography sets a mood of focused productivity.\n*   **Prompt Idea D:** \"A top-down, minimalist photo of a neat workspace corner. A matte ceramic coffee cup next to a sleek gray mechanical keyboard. Soft, warm morning light casting gentle shadows. Professional, calm, aesthetic.\"\n*   **Prompt Idea E:** \"A close-up of a person\'s hands holding a warm cup of tea, resting on a clean wooden desk. Soft natural lighting, shallow depth of field, cozy and productive atmosphere.\"\n\n### 3. Playful Minimalist Illustration (Friendly & Approachable)\nLine art or simple illustrations add character and reduce the \"corporate software\" feel.\n*   **Prompt Idea F:** \"A minimalist line-art illustration of a friendly, small bird carrying a tiny envelope. Drawn in a continuous, elegant dark gray line with a single pop of coral orange color. Clean white background.\"\n*   **Prompt Idea G:** \"A flat vector illustration of an intricate, chaotic knot of string instantly transforming into a perfectly straight line. Minimalist, using only slate gray and warm coral colors on an off-white background.\"\n\n**Where to put them?**\n*   **The \"No Matches Found\" State:** Replace the magnifying glass emoji with a small, rounded image of the minimalist bird or clay shapes.\n*   **A Header Banner:** Add a slim, wide image (like the frosted glass or folded paper) right between the category tabs and the first snippet card to break up the UI and add warmth.\n\nWould you like me to generate one of these using the image generation tool and place it into the app (e.g., as a banner or in the empty state)?"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 404493593
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
